{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-77008" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069622/assets/dea7eed9213ddf1bb3293950e2490b120a061e9add1172d3b850ccbc58f90454.png)\n\nEvaluate the line integral ${\\int }_{C}F(r)\\cdot \\text{d}r,$ where $F(x,y)=(y+x)\\,i+x\\,j$ and $C$ is the arc of the ellipse ${x}^{2}+4{y}^{2}=4$ traversed from the point $A(-2,0)$ to the point $B(0,-1).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069622/state.json" "file_sha256" "87c91e1ef9c28665dee4d1482bb074154c7ea44ce9f7c3a58d9eaf46bf2643e0"} {"question" "q-77008" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r={\\int }_{a}^{b}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to parameterize the curve. Notice that we can write its equation as\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+{y}^{2}=1.\n$$\n\nSo, our curve is a part-ellipse centered at the origin with horizontal and vertical semiaxes $2$ and $1$ respectively. This curve can be parameterized as\n\n$$\nr(t)=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j,\\,\\pi \\le t\\le \\frac{3\\pi }{2}.\n$$\n\nSo, along the curve $C,$ we have\n\n$$\nx=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡t.\n$$\n\nAs a result, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t)) & =(y+x)\\,i+x\\,j \\\\  & =(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)\\,i+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing ${r}^{′}(t),$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)j \\\\  & =-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t) & =((\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)\\,i+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j)\\cdot (-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j) \\\\  & =(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)\\cdot (-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\  & =-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+2(-{sin}^{2}⁡t+{cos}^{2}⁡t) \\\\  & =-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can evaluate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}F(r)\\cdot \\text{d}r & ={\\int }_{\\pi }^{3\\pi /2}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi }^{3\\pi /2}(-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t)\\,dt \\\\  & =[\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t+\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t]_{\\pi }^{3\\pi /2} \\\\  & =[-1+0]-[1-0] \\\\  & =-2\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069622/state.json" "file_sha256" "87c91e1ef9c28665dee4d1482bb074154c7ea44ce9f7c3a58d9eaf46bf2643e0"} {"question" "q-77008" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069622/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "ce3e1ef8f2b83fde41f11b9866321432f38268bd50832154b2c84b202cda916e"} {"question" "q-77008" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069622/state.json" "file_sha256" "87c91e1ef9c28665dee4d1482bb074154c7ea44ce9f7c3a58d9eaf46bf2643e0"} {"question" "q-77008" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-2"] ["math" "0"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "2-\\frac{2\\pi }{3}"] ["math" "\\pi -2"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069622/state.json" "file_sha256" "87c91e1ef9c28665dee4d1482bb074154c7ea44ce9f7c3a58d9eaf46bf2643e0"} {"question" "q-77008" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-2"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069622/state.json" "file_sha256" "87c91e1ef9c28665dee4d1482bb074154c7ea44ce9f7c3a58d9eaf46bf2643e0"} {"question" "q-77032" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069622/assets/08c3195e7325d853f61562b1f62460cb0796f14377286228f2b7cd40983202ac.png)\n\nEvaluate the line integral ${\\int }_{C}F(r)\\cdot \\text{d}r,$ where $F(x,y)=3\\,i+\\frac{1}{x}\\,j$ and $C$ is the arc of the circle ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=16$  traversed from the point $A(4,0)$ to the point $B(0,4).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069622/state.json" "file_sha256" "87c91e1ef9c28665dee4d1482bb074154c7ea44ce9f7c3a58d9eaf46bf2643e0"} {"question" "q-77032" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r={\\int }_{a}^{b}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to parameterize a circle of radius $4$ centered at the origin. It can be parameterized as \n\n$$\nr(t)=4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i+4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j,\\,0\\le t\\le \\frac{\\pi }{2}.\n$$\n\nSo, along the curve $C,$ we have\n\n$$\nx=4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,y=4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t.\n$$\n\nAs a result,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t)) & =3\\,i+\\frac{1}{x}\\,j \\\\  & =3\\,i+\\frac{1}{4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing ${r}^{′}(t),$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)j \\\\  & =-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t) & =(3\\,i+\\frac{1}{4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}\\,j)\\cdot (-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j) \\\\  & =3\\cdot (-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)+\\frac{1}{4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}\\cdot 4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\  & =-12\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can evaluate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}F(r)\\cdot \\text{d}r & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}(-12\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+1)\\,dt \\\\  & =[12\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+t]_{0}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =(0+\\frac{\\pi }{2})-(12+0) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{2}-12\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069622/state.json" "file_sha256" "87c91e1ef9c28665dee4d1482bb074154c7ea44ce9f7c3a58d9eaf46bf2643e0"} {"question" "q-77032" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069622/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "ce3e1ef8f2b83fde41f11b9866321432f38268bd50832154b2c84b202cda916e"} {"question" "q-77032" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069622/state.json" "file_sha256" "87c91e1ef9c28665dee4d1482bb074154c7ea44ce9f7c3a58d9eaf46bf2643e0"} {"question" "q-77032" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-12"] ["math" "12-\\frac{\\pi }{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\pi }{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\pi }{2}-12"] ["math" "\\pi -12"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069622/state.json" "file_sha256" "87c91e1ef9c28665dee4d1482bb074154c7ea44ce9f7c3a58d9eaf46bf2643e0"} {"question" "q-77032" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{\\pi }{2}-12"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069622/state.json" "file_sha256" "87c91e1ef9c28665dee4d1482bb074154c7ea44ce9f7c3a58d9eaf46bf2643e0"} {"question" "q-125047" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following is equivalent to ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r,$ where $F(x,y)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+y)\\,i+\\sqrt{xy}\\,j$ and $C$ is the line segment traversed from the point $A(1,1)$ to the point $B(4,3)?$\n\n*Hint: Use the parametrization $r(t)=(1+3t)\\,i+(1+2t)\\,j.$*" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069622/state.json" "file_sha256" "87c91e1ef9c28665dee4d1482bb074154c7ea44ce9f7c3a58d9eaf46bf2643e0"} {"question" "q-125047" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r={\\int }_{a}^{b}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to parameterize the line segment.\nThe position vectors of the endpoints of our line segment are \n$a=i+j$ and $b=4\\,i+3\\,j.$\nSo, the parametrization of the line segment is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =a+t(b-a) \\\\  & =(i+j)+t[(4\\,i+3\\,j)-(i+j)] \\\\  & =(i+j)+t(3i+2\\,j) \\\\  & =(1+3t)\\,i+(1+2t)\\,j,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t$ varies from $t=0$ (at the point $A$) to $t=1$ (at the point $B$).\nThus, along the curve $C,$ we have\n\n$$\nx=1+3t,\\,y=1+2t.\n$$\n\nAs a result, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t)) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+y)\\,i+\\sqrt{xy}\\,j \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1+3t+1+2t)\\,i+\\sqrt{(1+3t)(1+2t)}\\,j \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2+5t)\\,i+\\sqrt{1+5t+6{t}^{2}}\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing ${r}^{′}(t),$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(1+3t)i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(1+2t)j \\\\  & =3\\,i+2\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t) & =(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2+5t)\\,i+\\sqrt{1+5t+6{t}^{2}}\\,j)\\cdot (3\\,i+2\\,j) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2+5t)\\cdot 3+\\sqrt{1+5t+6{t}^{2}}\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =3\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2+5t)+2\\sqrt{1+5t+6{t}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can write the integral as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}3\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2+5t)+2\\sqrt{1+5t+6{t}^{2}}\\,dt.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069622/state.json" "file_sha256" "87c91e1ef9c28665dee4d1482bb074154c7ea44ce9f7c3a58d9eaf46bf2643e0"} {"question" "q-125047" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069622/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "ce3e1ef8f2b83fde41f11b9866321432f38268bd50832154b2c84b202cda916e"} {"question" "q-125047" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069622/state.json" "file_sha256" "87c91e1ef9c28665dee4d1482bb074154c7ea44ce9f7c3a58d9eaf46bf2643e0"} {"question" "q-125047" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{\\int }_{0}^{1}2\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5t)+3\\sqrt{6}t\\,dt"] ["math" "{\\int }_{0}^{1}3\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2+5t)+2\\sqrt{1+5t+6{t}^{2}}\\,dt"] ["math" "{\\int }_{0}^{1}5\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2+5t)+6\\sqrt{1+5t+6{t}^{2}}\\,dt"] ["math" "{\\int }_{0}^{1}5\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5t)+6\\sqrt{6}t\\,dt"] ["math" "{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2+5t)+\\sqrt{1+5t+6{t}^{2}}\\,dt"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069622/state.json" "file_sha256" "87c91e1ef9c28665dee4d1482bb074154c7ea44ce9f7c3a58d9eaf46bf2643e0"} {"question" "q-125047" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{\\int }_{0}^{1}3\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2+5t)+2\\sqrt{1+5t+6{t}^{2}}\\,dt"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069622/state.json" "file_sha256" "87c91e1ef9c28665dee4d1482bb074154c7ea44ce9f7c3a58d9eaf46bf2643e0"} {"question" "q-125065" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r,$ where $F(x,y)=x\\,i+2y\\,j$ and $C$ is the curve $\\operatorname{ln}⁡y-x=0$ traversed from the point $A(0,1)$ to the point $B(1,e).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069622/state.json" "file_sha256" "87c91e1ef9c28665dee4d1482bb074154c7ea44ce9f7c3a58d9eaf46bf2643e0"} {"question" "q-125065" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r={\\int }_{a}^{b}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to parameterize the curve. Making $x$ the subject of the equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{ln}⁡y-x=0\\,⟹\\,x=\\operatorname{ln}⁡y.\n$$\n\nSo, the parametrization of the curve is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡t\\,i+t\\,j,\\,1\\le t\\le e.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, along the curve $C,$ we have\n\n$$\nx=\\operatorname{ln}⁡t,\\,y=t.\n$$\n\nAs a result, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t)) & =x\\,i+2y\\,j \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡t\\,i+2t\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing ${r}^{′}(t),$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)j \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{t}\\,i+j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t) & =(\\operatorname{ln}⁡t\\,i+2t\\,j)\\cdot (\\frac{1}{t}\\,i+j) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡t\\cdot \\frac{1}{t}+2t\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡t}{t}+2t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r & ={\\int }_{1}^{e}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{e}(\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡t}{t}+2t)\\,dt \\\\  & ={[\\frac{{ln}^{2}⁡t}{2}+{t}^{2}]}_{1}^{e} \\\\  & =(\\frac{{ln}^{2}⁡e}{2}+{e}^{2})-(0+1) \\\\  & ={e}^{2}-\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069622/state.json" "file_sha256" "87c91e1ef9c28665dee4d1482bb074154c7ea44ce9f7c3a58d9eaf46bf2643e0"} {"question" "q-125065" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069622/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "ce3e1ef8f2b83fde41f11b9866321432f38268bd50832154b2c84b202cda916e"} {"question" "q-125065" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069622/state.json" "file_sha256" "87c91e1ef9c28665dee4d1482bb074154c7ea44ce9f7c3a58d9eaf46bf2643e0"} {"question" "q-125065" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{e-1}{2}"] ["math" "e+\\frac{1}{2}"] ["math" "e-\\frac{1}{2}"] ["math" "{e}^{2}+\\frac{1}{2}"] ["math" "{e}^{2}-\\frac{1}{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069622/state.json" "file_sha256" "87c91e1ef9c28665dee4d1482bb074154c7ea44ce9f7c3a58d9eaf46bf2643e0"} {"question" "q-125065" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{e}^{2}-\\frac{1}{2}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069622/state.json" "file_sha256" "87c91e1ef9c28665dee4d1482bb074154c7ea44ce9f7c3a58d9eaf46bf2643e0"} {"question" "q-125119" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following is equivalent to the integral ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r,$ where $F(x,y)=2y\\,i+{x}^{2}\\,j$ and $C$ is the curve $\\sqrt{y}=x+3$ traversed from the point $A(-3,0)$ to the point $B(-1,4)?$\n\n*Hint: Use the parametrization $r(t)=(\\sqrt{t}-3)\\,i+t\\,j.$*" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069622/state.json" "file_sha256" "87c91e1ef9c28665dee4d1482bb074154c7ea44ce9f7c3a58d9eaf46bf2643e0"} {"question" "q-125119" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r={\\int }_{a}^{b}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to parameterize the curve. This is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =(\\sqrt{t}-3)\\,i+t\\,j,\\,0\\le t\\le 4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, along the curve $C,$ we have\n\n$$\nx=\\sqrt{t}-3,\\,y=t.\n$$\n\nAs a result, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t)) & =2t\\,i+(\\sqrt{t}-3)^{2}\\,j \\\\  & =2t\\,i+(t-6\\sqrt{t}+9)\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing ${r}^{′}(t),$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\sqrt{t}-3)i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)j \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{t}}\\,i+j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t) & =(2t\\,i+(t-6\\sqrt{t}+9)\\,j)\\cdot (\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{t}}\\,i+j) \\\\  & =2t\\cdot \\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{t}}+t-6\\sqrt{t}+9 \\\\  & =\\sqrt{t}+t-6\\sqrt{t}+9 \\\\  & =t-5\\sqrt{t}+9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can write the integral as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}(t-5\\sqrt{t}+9)\\,dt.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069622/state.json" "file_sha256" "87c91e1ef9c28665dee4d1482bb074154c7ea44ce9f7c3a58d9eaf46bf2643e0"} {"question" "q-125119" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069622/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "ce3e1ef8f2b83fde41f11b9866321432f38268bd50832154b2c84b202cda916e"} {"question" "q-125119" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069622/state.json" "file_sha256" "87c91e1ef9c28665dee4d1482bb074154c7ea44ce9f7c3a58d9eaf46bf2643e0"} {"question" "q-125119" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{\\int }_{0}^{4}(t+5\\sqrt{t}+3)\\,dt"] ["math" "{\\int }_{0}^{4}(t+6\\sqrt{t}+9)\\,dt"] ["